# ── Runtime state and secrets: never part of a build ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# WHY THESE MATTER, not just tidiness:
#
# 1. data/ is live validator state — CometBFT databases, replay stores — and it changes every second.
#    The Dockerfile does `COPY . ./`, so a changing data/ invalidates that layer on EVERY build, and
#    each of the seven validator images then rebuilds the expensive CGO `go build` from scratch instead
#    of reusing cache. Measured 2026-09-18: a 22.3 MB context and a full rebuild per service.
#
# 2. .env.shared holds DATABASE_URL (with the password) and ETH_PRIVATE_KEY. It was NOT matched by the
#    existing `.env` / `.env.local` rules, so it was being shipped to the daemon and written into the
#    builder stage. The final image is clean — the production stage copies only named artifacts — but a
#    secret has no business in a build context or a layer cache at all.
#
# NOT excluded, deliberately: bls_zk_keys/ and bls_zk_keys_bls12381*/ are COPYed out of the builder into
# the final image (Dockerfile ~line 130). Excluding them produces an image that cannot prove anything.
data/
bft-keys/
.env.shared
.env.shared.*
*.bak
*.bak[0-9]
*.bak-*
*.bak.*
